# DataLad / git-annex (ADR-2605241500): the bounded R0 EDN snapshot is git-tracked
# directly (small, single raw block). The full-world bulk corpus (PatentsView TSV /
# EPO / WIPO, the operator G9 ingest) is annexed → IPFS, not committed to git.
* annex.largefiles=(largerthan=256kb)
*.kotoba.edn -filter -text annex.largefiles=nothing
*.edn -filter annex.largefiles=nothing
README.md -filter annex.largefiles=nothing
PUBLISH.md -filter annex.largefiles=nothing
# bulk pulls (annexed → IPFS, never inline in git)
*.tsv filter=annex
*.tsv.zip filter=annex
*.raw.edn filter=annex
* annex.backend=MD5E
**/.git* annex.largefiles=nothing
# The harvest journal — append-only quads, one per line, sharded at 1 MiB.
#
# Git-tracked, NOT annexed, and that is a decision rather than an omission: a
# sealed shard is byte-identical forever, so git stores it exactly once, and
# keeping it in git preserves `git diff` / `git blame` on the artifact that
# ADR-2607072300 designates as THE authoritative record. Annexing it would buy
# nothing at 1 MiB a shard and cost the review surface.
#
# The annex is for what git is genuinely bad at: the bulk operator pulls below,
# which arrive as single multi-gigabyte files with no useful line structure.
80-data/public/*.journal.edn -filter annex.largefiles=nothing
